# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Neither of these may ever be committed.
# Both contain the owner's real financial positions and personal context:
# holdings with weights, concentration, location, and employer details.
# docs/brief.md is the project spec and CLAUDE.md tells you to put it there --
# keep it locally, but it stays out of git. Nothing in the codebase reads either
# file at build or test time, so their absence breaks nothing for a clone.
docs/brief.md
config/portfolio.yaml

# A corrupted AGENTS.md mirror, moved out of the repo root on 2026-08-14.
# Kept rather than deleted (standing rule: nothing is deleted, obsolete files go
# to attic/), but kept OUT of git, the same way the archived first-run database
# in attic/ is -- present on this machine, absent from a clone.
#
# It was a stale copy of CLAUDE.md from mid-M1 with "claude" string-replaced by
# "Codex", which corrupted the three places that word appears inside a real path
# or package name: it told the reader the deny list lives at .Codex/settings.json
# and the skills come from superpowers@Codex-plugins-official. Neither exists.
#
# AGENTS.md is a real convention that some agent tooling reads as authoritative,
# and this file was NOT gitignored while it sat at the repo root -- so it was
# both readable as instructions and one `git add -A` away from being committed
# as if it were guidance.
#
# CORRECTION, 2026-08-14 evening: the paragraph that used to sit here said "no
# hook, script, or plugin generates it ... so it will not reappear on its own."
# That was wrong, and a fresh corrupt copy appeared at the repo root the same
# day, timestamped DURING an active session. The original investigation searched
# this repo's settings, user-scope Claude settings, and plugins -- all correctly,
# and all in the wrong place.
#
# The generator is OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT.app). `AGENTS.md` is Codex's own
# instruction-file convention, the way CLAUDE.md is Claude's, and it mirrors
# CLAUDE.md into it with a vendor-name substitution. That substitution is what
# corrupts the three places "claude" appears inside a real path or package name.
# Evidence: ~/.codex/ holds sessions referencing this repo by name, plus a
# claude-cowork-import-history.json, and com.openai.codex processes run on this
# machine. Nothing in Claude's configuration is involved, which is exactly why
# searching Claude's configuration found nothing.
#
# So the repo-root path is now ignored rather than left free: it will keep being
# regenerated, and each regeneration is a corrupt instruction file in a PUBLIC
# repo's root. A deliberately-authored AGENTS.md can still be committed with
# `git add -f`. CLAUDE.md remains the authority either way.
/AGENTS.md
attic/AGENTS.md.corrupt-2026-08-14

# A stray, byte-identical duplicate of src/score/overrides.ts that was written
# to the repo ROOT by mistake during M2 task 6. Dead where it landed — its
# `../domain/item.ts` import only resolves from src/score/ — and moved to attic/
# rather than deleted, per the standing never-delete rule.
#
# Note for anyone reasoning about attic/: it is NOT blanket-gitignored. Only
# specific patterns are (`*.db`, `*.db-wal`, `*.db-shm` above), which is why the
# archived first-run database sits there untracked while a stray .ts would not.
# Each non-matching file put there needs its own line here, or it stays visible
# in `git status` as an untracked file forever.
attic/overrides.ts.stray-2026-08-14

# A sed backup left by a mutation-testing step during M3 task 5. Preserved
# (never delete) but kept out of git, like the other attic strays above.
attic/sources.ts.bak2-mutation-test-2026-08-14

